ded years, week-year boundaries, defaults, invalid input, formatting, and round-trips.\n- **Times and datetimes:** parse, format and round-trip, including fractions and time zones.\n- **Time zones:** `FixedOffset`, `UTC`, local time, and `tz_isoformat`.\n- **Durations:** `parse_duration`, `duration_isoformat`, and the `Duration` class (arithmetic, equality, hashing, `totimedelta`, pickling, string forms).\n\nNo test failed because of a library bug. My first run had 6 failures, and each was a wrong expectation of mine about what the library does, so I changed the tests to match the library's actual behaviour. Those behaviours are the quirks below, and the suite does not flag them as bugs:\n- `parse_date(\"2003-366\")` returns 2004-01-01 instead of raising.\n- `parse_tzinfo(\"abc\")` returns `None`.\n- `parse_duration(\"PT\")` and `\"P1D\\n\"` are accepted.\n- Year 0000 in the alternative duration format raises `ValueError`.\n- Formatting a plain `timedelta` with `%Y` or `%m` raises `AttributeError`.","ttft_ms":2402,"type":"result","duration_ms":130807,"uuid":"46906c82-2481-4111-ade9-a8db3168ed83","ttft_stream_ms":1277,"time_to_request_ms":165,"first_content_frame_ms":1277,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

